  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member using background checks, I want each new MP or flagged topic to notify me once, so that I am not notified twice for the same news.\n\n### Scope\n\nPer-account ledger: last notified MP unread count and thread ids, per-topic last notified last-post stamp for flags, last check date (for the minimum interval). Pure value logic + persistence protocol, file and in-memory implementations.\n\n- Module: HFRStorage · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-005 (#149)\n- Absorbs: FEATURES.md FEAT-005 'already notified state (HFRStorage)'\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `MPBackgroundService.swift:70-110` (legacy compares the MP count with the last one notified)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-091-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-013 (#46, done)\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-005 (#149), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-092 (#184), LOT-141 (#231); the last lot (LOT-141 (#231)) closes #149.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `diff(summary:)` returns only items not yet notified; `record` is idempotent.\n- [ ] Last check date stored; `isDue(now:minimumInterval:)` tested at the boundary.\n- [ ] Account removal drops the ledger of that account.\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-091-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
