   "body": "**Ready for outside contributors** (steward `ext/opus-helper1`, operator decision 2026-10-29) · milestone ⚙️ M3 (board #324)\n\n**Before you start, read** (on `dev-swift`):\n- [AGENTS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/AGENTS.md): the rules and the definition of done (§9)\n- [docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md): claims, review and merge for outside contributors\n- [docs/agents/LESSONS.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/agents/LESSONS.md): the self-review table\n- [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), [docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md), [docs/FIXTURES.md](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/FIXTURES.md)\n- the LOTS.md row of this lot, and its dependencies: LOT-013 ([#46](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/46), done; spec [LOT-013](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/lots/LOT-013-account-settings-mpstorage.md)); also [ADR 0013](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/adr/0013-storage-tiers.md) (the ledger is device-only, per account key)\n\n**Spec:** you write `docs/lots/LOT-091-<name>.md` first (AGENTS.md §5 step 2), from this issue's scope, sources and acceptance criteria. This issue body is complete (scope, legacy `MPBackgroundService.swift:70-110`, acceptance criteria). Gaps: (1) the input of `diff(summary:)` (MP unread count and thread ids, flagged topics with their last-post stamp) is not a type yet; the check flow is the sibling lot LOT-092 ([#184](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/184)), so define the smallest value type in HFRStorage or reuse existing HFRModels types (`PrivateMessageThread`, `TopicSummary`), and ask on the issue before adding any public HFRModels type (core-model guard); (2) copy the persistence pattern of the existing stores (`PseudoListPersistence` with file and in-memory implementations under `HFRStorage/PseudoLists/`); (3) the per-account key and account removal follow ADR 0013 §7 and LOT-065. No HFR capture is needed (pure value logic). Feature umbrella FEAT-005 ([#149](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/149), proposed by Bybifok: credit in the spec, the PR and CREDITS.md); umbrellas are never claimed: the PR says `Closes #183` and `Refs #149`.\n\n**Claim:** `/claim ext/<you>-<model>-<n>`, or `CLAIM REQUEST` if you have no write access (EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §5). The first claim wins.\n\n**Routing:** Sonnet → Opus (LOTS.md). The adversarial review may be run by **another agent of yours**, as long as it uses a different model (AGENTS.md §6).\n\n**Merge:** if you have no write access, the steward merges after the APPROVE and green CI. Every lot delivered by an outside contributor is also listed for the final Fable audit (#326).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
